From c47acdaf3bb6e5fe669864e063cfa5e39108848e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:37:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 51/53] SMB requests time out after 5 s; a lost SMB connection
 gives NOT READY and reconnects in the background

libsmb2's default timeout is 0, so a sync call waits until the server answers. The HDS reads and
writes run in the USB task, so a slow or blocked SMB server held one USB command past the host's
30 s SCSI timeout; the host reset the device, and when the call returned TinyUSB panicked
(ep 01 was already available).

Every SMB context now gets smb2_set_timeout(5). When an HDS read/write or the keepalive fails,
smb_lost() marks the connection down (a timed-out request's late reply would break the libsmb2
context anyway) and asks the connect task to reconnect; it retries every 5 s until the HDS opens.
Until then the HDS answers NOT READY (02/04/01) without touching SMB, and the host retries. The
HDS I/O also takes remote_sem without waiting, so it never uses a context the connect task is
tearing down. vd_unmount_smb lowers sysstatus before the (slow) disconnect, so the HDS never
answers MEDIUM ERROR in between.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
